                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Patrick Williams",
                        "email": "patrick@stwcx.xyz",
                        "username": "williamspatrick"
                    },
                    "message": "I hope this is all temporary workarounds.  We shouldn't really be relying on phosphor-virtual-sensors here for \"status\" and phosphor-pid-control should handle any power states and/or missing states as-required by your platform.  If it isn't supported already, we should add code to do so.\n\nIt seems like we've coded up hundreds of lines of YAML/JSON, bitbake config, shell scripts, and service files, just to avoid writing under 50 lines of code in phosphor-pid-control."
                }
